Expected elements: present

All backbone items are there and legible. The identity bar carries `← aztec`, the truncated hash, `Partial`, `block 101`, both stepping directions, the scrubber, `128 / 1315`, the `FETCHING·OPENING·POSITIONING` rail and two right-hand actions. No provenance band above the bar — provenance is now the `DATA` row in the Transaction pane with a `Synthetic demo data` badge and the producer's own sentences. `CODE`, `CALL TRACE | EVENT LOG` (Call Trace open), `VALUES` and `TRANSACTION` all present; current position is line 32.

Typographically this is a coherent tool. Pane titles are one tracked all-caps level, code is one monospace face, the ACIR column and the Values column are tabular and right-aligned across four magnitudes.

Three things are below bar. The provenance paragraph is set flush-right over eight lines while the two other prose blocks in the same pane (EXECUTIONS, SELECTOR) are flush-left — the register's most important claim is the one paragraph you must hunt the line-start for. FEE PAYER and TARGET wrap a 42-character address mid-byte across two lines instead of using the ellipsis convention the identity bar uses. And `⊙` versus `⊘` in the code gutter differ by a 1–2px interior mark at this size, so "ran" and "did not run" are carried by almost nothing.

Fixes: set the DATA paragraph flush-left with the pane's other prose; truncate FEE PAYER/TARGET rather than wrapping.

Rating: 7/10

